Your program is given these modules, each grouping the methods of one capability.
Each is a class of `static` methods, so you call one with
`<module>.<method>(args...)`. They are in scope already, through the `import`
lines gg writes into your program's header.

{{#each apis}}
- `{{object}}`: {{description}}
{{/each}}

One call tells you what a function does.

`{{api.view.open_docs_view.signature}}` **opens a view** directly, of one
method's full signature, documentation, and the types it uses. Pass its name
(`{{api.view.open_docs_view.call}}("{{api.view.open_text.name}}")`).

You are reading a view, so what you asked for arrives on your next
turn and is not available during the turn you ask for it. Ask in one turn, use it
in the next.

{{#if programLibrary}}
### Reusing a program you already ran

gg keeps the source of every program you run. `{{api.programs.get.call}}()` returns the last
one; `{{api.programs.get.call}}(turn)` returns the one from that turn, and
`{{api.programs.history.call}}()` lists the turns it still holds.

Use this when a program was nearly right. Fetch it, patch it as a `String`, and
hand it back with `{{api.programs.rerun.call}}(source)` — gg runs what you hand over as this
turn's program, so a one-character fix costs one line instead of the whole
program again:

```
String source = {{api.programs.get.call}}();
{{api.programs.rerun.call}}(source.replace("int totl = 1;", "int total = 1;"));
```

Everything the handing-over program already did stands, so hand over before
doing work you do not want done twice. Hand over once per turn: the first
hand-over is the one that runs.
{{/if}}

